{"title":"Amos","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Amos"},"headingText":"Amos","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\n::: {.book-summary}\n## Book Summary Insight\n\nAmos proclaims God's demand for justice, righteousness, and sincere worship. The book teaches that religious activity without obedience is unacceptable to God.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 1\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 1:3</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">For three transgressions and for four</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nRepeated prophetic formula\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter begins with judgments against Israel's surrounding nations. The key verse emphasizes that God holds all peoples accountable for their actions.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 2\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 2:7</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">They pant after the dust of the earth</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nSocial injustice condemned\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter continues judgments against the nations and turns specifically to Judah and Israel. The key verse highlights Israel's guilt despite receiving God's blessings and revelation.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 3\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 3:3</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Can two walk together, except they be agreed?</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nOne of Amos' most quoted verses\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter explains why God is judging Israel. The key verse emphasizes that privilege brings responsibility and accountability before God.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 4\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 4:12</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Prepare to meet thy God</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nFamous prophetic warning\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter recounts God's repeated attempts to bring Israel to repentance. The key verse reveals that God's discipline was intended to lead His people back to Him.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 5\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 5:24</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Let judgment run down as waters</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nOne of the most cited justice passages in Scripture\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter calls Israel to seek the Lord and live. The key verse emphasizes genuine righteousness rather than empty religious observance.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 6\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 6:1</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Woe to them that are at ease in Zion</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nWarning against complacency\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter condemns complacency and self-indulgence. The key verse warns against false security amid spiritual decline.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 7\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 7:8</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">A plumb line in the midst of My people</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nFamous prophetic image\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records visions of coming judgment and Amos's confrontation with Amaziah. The key verse highlights the prophet's faithfulness in delivering God's message.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 8\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 8:11</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">A famine of hearing the words of the LORD</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nFrequently quoted verse\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter contains the vision of the basket of summer fruit. The key verse warns of a coming famine of hearing God's word.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 9\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 9:11</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">I will raise up the tabernacle of David</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nQuoted in Acts 15\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter concludes with judgment followed by restoration. The key verse promises the future rebuilding and blessing of God's people.\n:::\n\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n# Amos\n\n::: {.book-summary}\n## Book Summary Insight\n\nAmos proclaims God's demand for justice, righteousness, and sincere worship. The book teaches that religious activity without obedience is unacceptable to God.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 1\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 1:3</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">For three transgressions and for four</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nRepeated prophetic formula\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter begins with judgments against Israel's surrounding nations. The key verse emphasizes that God holds all peoples accountable for their actions.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 2\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 2:7</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">They pant after the dust of the earth</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nSocial injustice condemned\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter continues judgments against the nations and turns specifically to Judah and Israel. The key verse highlights Israel's guilt despite receiving God's blessings and revelation.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 3\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 3:3</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Can two walk together, except they be agreed?</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nOne of Amos' most quoted verses\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter explains why God is judging Israel. The key verse emphasizes that privilege brings responsibility and accountability before God.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 4\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 4:12</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Prepare to meet thy God</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nFamous prophetic warning\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter recounts God's repeated attempts to bring Israel to repentance. The key verse reveals that God's discipline was intended to lead His people back to Him.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 5\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 5:24</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Let judgment run down as waters</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nOne of the most cited justice passages in Scripture\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter calls Israel to seek the Lord and live. The key verse emphasizes genuine righteousness rather than empty religious observance.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 6\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 6:1</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Woe to them that are at ease in Zion</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nWarning against complacency\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter condemns complacency and self-indulgence. The key verse warns against false security amid spiritual decline.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 7\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 7:8</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">A plumb line in the midst of My people</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nFamous prophetic image\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records visions of coming judgment and Amos's confrontation with Amaziah. The key verse highlights the prophet's faithfulness in delivering God's message.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 8\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 8:11</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">A famine of hearing the words of the LORD</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nFrequently quoted verse\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter contains the vision of the basket of summer fruit. The key verse warns of a coming famine of hearing God's word.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 9\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Amos 9:11</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">I will raise up the tabernacle of David</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nQuoted in Acts 15\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter concludes with judgment followed by restoration. The key verse promises the future rebuilding and blessing of God's people.\n:::\n\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],